Monolithic vs Microservices: Real-Time DevOps Interview Scenarios

Preparing for DevOps interviews? Here's how real-world problems are tackled in both architectures:

Monolithic Architecture
Deployment failure in one module → impacts the whole app
Scaling a single feature → requires scaling the entire monolith
Zero-downtime deployment → needs blue/green strategy & session handling

Microservices Architecture
One service fails → isolate with retries, circuit breakers
Shared data across services → use APIs or event-driven updates
Service discovery in Kubernetes → handled via DNS or service mesh
CI/CD pipelines → one per service using Docker, Helm, GitOps
Logging & Monitoring → centralized with ELK/EFK, Prometheus, Grafana
Rollbacks → easy with versioned deployments and health checks

These scenarios are common in interviews and actual production setups.
 Understanding them helps you move beyond theory and into real DevOps problem-solving.
